A||||6||REDHOTT88||88 Formula shifting||||8||
Z||000000||REDHOTT88||11-16-2001||03:19 PM||||I just bought an 88 Fiero Formula. It shifts fine when moving, but it's hard to put into 1st at a stop. I sometimes have to take off in 2nd. Has new clutch, doesn't have problems in other gears. Any Advice?||||reg||8
Z||000001||LZeitgeist||11-16-2001||03:28 PM||||Bleed the clutch hydraulic system... check the clutch master cylinder and the clutch slave cylinder for leaks, as well as the connections going to each of them... (the slave cylinder seems to crack on the underside more often than other areas, in my experience...)<P>It sounds to me like you have a bit of air in the hydraulic system which isn't giving you the full release throw on the clutch, so things are still turning and grabbing just a bit when you try to put it in first while standing still.<P>Welcome to the Formula Family!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Patrick W. Heinske  --  LZeitgeist@aol.com<BR>1988 Red Fiero Formula<BR>- 1st Place - Stock Coupe - FOCOSEVA 2000<BR>- 3rd Place - Stock Formula - FOCOA Nat'l 2001<BR>- Class Winner - 1982 to Present - 2001 Tarheel Tigers All-Pontiac Show||||reg||1
Z||000002||fldevel||11-16-2001||03:45 PM||||check tranny fluid level .. tends to shift hard into 1st and 3rd when fluid levels are low .. would save you the trouble of bleeding the clutch  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||LZeitgeist||11-16-2001||03:54 PM||||Bleeding the clutch would save him the trouble of checking the tranny fluid level.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>(Just kidding... sounds like a possibility as well.)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||Hardworker||11-18-2001||11:58 PM||||Had the first gear problem with my 88 Formula.  Tried 3 different brands of syn oil in attempt to cure problem.  Ended up putting in the syncromesh xmission fluid GM part# 12345349 and the first gear problem at stop lites/signs went away.<P>Love those 88s||||reg||1
Z||000005||Brandon86SE||11-19-2001||12:28 AM||||I was having a similar problem with it being hard to get into 1st, and reverse.  What was the case for me was that the plate connecting the shift cable to the tranny was missing a bolt, and the other one was nearly off!  I couldn't believe it, and still don't know how on earth that happened!  Once I got a couple new bolts in it it's been better, less flopping around back there.<P>Brandon<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Field_Front_(sig)_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Alex4mula||11-19-2001||09:04 AM||||I had that problem. If the rest of the shifts are ok then maybe the 1st gear syncro is gone. Very common and very $$$ to fix. Make sure your hrydraulics are ok and put that syncromesh xmission fluid mentioned above. Made a big difference for me.<P>------------------<BR>    Alex4mula<BR>:) Red-Original Owner & White-1/94 with PM (:||||reg||1
